WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.080
Every tutorial about AI coding has the same problem.

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:06.360
You watch someone do it on their machine, and then you close the tab

3
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.760
and try it on yours.

4
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:10.640
Most of what you learned doesn't survive the trip.

5
00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:13.000
Tessl Academy is our attempt at fixing that.

6
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.360
It's a hands-on curriculum for getting more out of the agent you already use.

7
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:19.200
And every lesson works two ways.

8
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.120
Read it on the site like an article, or install the course

9
00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:26.000
and have your own coding agent walk you through it on your own repository.

10
00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:29.320
Same ground, but only one of them leaves you with working code.

11
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:33.320
You'll write your first skill, watch your agent reach for it unprompted,

12
00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.800
put a number on whether it's any good, and then teach the reviewer

13
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.120
the conventions your team keeps in its head.

14
00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:42.400
Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, or Tessl.

15
00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.200
Bring whichever you already use.

16
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.920
It's free. Start at tessl.io/academy.
